  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">DRG: PIDR Global Labor Program - Inclusive Futures (GLP-IF)</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">(USAID Bureau for Development, Democracy, and Innovation (D):  GLP-Inclusive Futures (GLP-IF) is implemented by a broad and diverse coalition of local and international institutions led by Sightsavers. GLP-IF tests an integrated systems approach for advancing the labor rights of people with disabilities, especially women, in Kenya. This approach could serve as a model for other contexts and other ultra-marginalized populations. Through GLP-IF, USAID will continue in Year-2 with FY 2022 funds to build relationships among workers, unions, non-governmental organizations, government, and companies to implement four interlocking workstreams:.1: Increasing access to decent work for persons with disabilities, particularly women workers - including in the climate-smart agriculture sector..2: Building the capacities of Kenyan trade unions and disabled persons&apos; organizations (DPOs) to increasingly support women and men with disabilities by promoting and protecting labor rights..3: Influencing and building capacities among brands and value chain employers to develop, apply and measure rights-respecting employment and operational policies..4: Policy advocacy with the Government of Kenya to improve labor rights legislation and enforcement..GLP-IF directly contributes to the Multilateral Partnership for Organizing, Worker Empowerment, and Rights (M-POWER) initiative, which is a key deliverable of the Presidential Initiative for Democratic Renewal (PIDR) that USAID collaborates on with the Department of Labor and U.S. Department of State&apos;s Bureau for Democracy, Rights, and Labor (DRL)..</narrative>
  </description>
